ompany\" and \"your company\" to avoid placeholders. But formal letter needs sender/recipient? Could include placeholders for names and dates only: e.g. [Date], [Vendor Contact Name], [Vendor Company Name]? Vendor company name is a name? It says names and dates, likely names of people and dates. But company names are names too? To be safe, use placeholders only for personal names and dates, and refer to companies descriptively: \"our company\" and \"your company\". But a formal letter usually has address. Could do:\n\n[Date]\n\n[Vendor Contact Name]\n[Vendor Company Name]\n...\n\nBut [Vendor Company Name] is a placeholder for a name (company name). Is that allowed? \"names and dates\" could include company names. But \"only for names and dates\" means no placeholders for GPU model, program name, etc. We can use [Vendor Company Name] as name. But maybe they want no bracketed placeholders except names/dates. We can include [Date], [Vendor Contact Name], [Vendor Company Name], [Your Name], [Your Title]. That's names and dates. Need about 350 words. Let's draft around 350.\n\nNeed state what company builds: open-source inference engine. Why access matters before launch: optimize runtime, validate drivers, performance, compatibility, avoid launch delays", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0018581715412437916], [1421, -7.003323078155518]], [[1144, -1.4782061043661088e-05], [1902, -11.726113319396973]], [[310, -0.40612494945526123], [4087, -1.1881722211837769]], [[5707, -0.7356458306312561], [4087, -1.1170239448547363]], [[310, -5.722062269342132e-06], [303, -12.720314025878906]], [[1156, -2.145769485650817e-06], [6163, -13.976316452026367]], [[25, -0.010899059474468231], [9859, -5.187845706939697]], [[328, -0.06761382520198822], [9357, -2.9270517826080322]], [[7734, -3.9697482861811295e-05], [2523, -10.74209976196289]], [[264, -3.445207767072134e-05], [15440, -11.091793060302734]], [[15440, -5.49569922441151e-05], [1304, -9.856267929077148]], [[6321, -7.033372639853042e-06], [15440, -1